## Product concept: “DataTrail”
A mobile app that collects limited usage/device data and sends it to a third-party analytics/telemetry service.

### Data collected
- App version
- Device model/OS
- Approx. region or city, only if location permission is granted
- Anonymous usage events: screen views, feature taps, session length
- Optional: battery/network type

### Not collected by default
- Name, email, phone number
- Contacts, photos, messages, precise location
- Free-text user input unless explicitly enabled

### Third party
Use a telemetry/analytics provider or your own backend. Example: `https://telemetry.example.com/v1/events`

### Flow
1. App asks for consent.
2. User chooses what to share.
3. App sends encrypted JSON over HTTPS.
4. Third party stores/processes data under a privacy policy.
5. User can view, delete, or opt out of data sharing.

